      "text": "Hecke algebras, generalisations and representation theory — 31 sections: Front matter; Algebras of Finite Type; Blocks\n\n**Hecke algebras, generalisations and representation theory**\n\n*The documents may come from teaching and research*\n\n75 pp, 31 sections.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Algebras of Finite Type; Blocks; Symmetrising forms and Schur elements; Decomposition maps; Iwahori–Hecke Algebras; Kazhdan–Lusztig cells; Schur elements and the a-function; Families of characters and Rouquier families; Decomposition maps and canonical basic sets; Cyclotomic Hecke Algebras; Hecke algebras for complex reflection groups; Schur elements and the a-function; Families of characters and Rouquier families; Decomposition maps and canonical basic sets; Ariki–Koike Algebras; Combinatorics of partitions and multipartition; Schur elements and the a-function",
